# Feature Modules & POS Micro-Features System

## Background

You already have the skeleton for this:
- A `ModuleRoute` component that gates pages based on `tenant.plan` (`pos_only`, `ecommerce_only`, `full_suite`)
- A `TenantPlan` enum on the backend

The problem: the current system is **too coarse** (3 plan strings) and has **no micro-feature support** inside pages (tax, credit, wholesale, discounts, etc.). The plan also doesn't match your real pricing tiers (Starter, Standard, Business, Ecom Only).

---

## The Industry Standard Approach

**Square, Toast, Lightspeed** all use a **two-layer feature system**:

```
Layer 1 — Module Access (Page-level gating)
  → "Can this tenant even open this page?"
  → Controlled by Plan + Add-ons
  → Example: Credit Ledger page only visible on Standard+

Layer 2 — Micro-Feature Flags (In-page behavior)
  → "What features are active inside this page?"
  → Controlled by Tenant Settings (independent of plan)
  → Example: Tax toggle in the POS register, wholesale pricing mode
```

The backend returns **one unified features object** at login. The frontend stores it and uses it everywhere.

---

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1**: Should POS micro-features (tax rate, credit mode, wholesale) be **owner-configurable** in Settings, or should they be locked per-plan and require an upgrade?
> - **Recommended**: Owner-configurable settings, but only unlocked at a certain plan tier.
> - Example: Tax is available on Standard+, but the owner turns it on/off in POS Settings.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q2**: The current `TenantPlan` enum (`pos_only`, `ecommerce_only`, `full_suite`) doesn't match your pricing image (Starter, Standard, Business, Ecom Only). Should we rename the enum values?
> - **Recommended**: Yes — rename to match pricing: `starter`, `standard`, `business`, `ecom_only`.
> - This is a **DB migration** change. Doable with a simple `ALTER TYPE`.

